title: Active play and asynchronous reflection substrate
---
flowchart TB
  accTitle: One active player acts while a background learner proposes evidence-linked procedures
  accDescr: One active player uses skills or ordinary input through the existing writer to windowed CDDA. Original receipts feed a bounded job mailbox. An advisory agent claims jobs and returns source linked proposals outside all input locks. Only the active player adopts procedure revisions through the existing memory writer. User Pause remains independent. Bounded actual overlap is demonstrated; general usefulness, apparent cadence and the integrated campaign remain separate acceptance questions.
  P["Active player<br/>plan, act, observe, correct"] --> I["Skills or direct interaction"]
  I --> W["One existing input writer"]
  W --> G["Windowed CDDA"]
  G --> E["Canonical visible evidence<br/>receipts and unfinished Work"]
  E --> P
  E -. "Original cutoff, age, horizon credits and omissions" .-> Q["Bounded cached jobs<br/>software idle wait, durable claim"]
  Q -. "No input lock or model wait" .-> R["Advisory agent<br/>author semantics and code<br/>software binds metadata"]
  R -. "Compact indexed candidates<br/>exact detail on demand" .-> P
  P -. "Automatic use and outcome links<br/>optional interpretation" .-> E
  P --> M["Explicitly selected candidate<br/>existing memory writer"]
  M --> E
  U["User Pause"] --> W
  classDef learner fill:#eef2ff,stroke:#4f46e5,color:#111827
  class R learner
